<title>FINLAND: Poll shows Finns still divided on EMU.</title>
<headline>Poll shows Finns still divided on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forty four percent of Finns oppose joining the European economic and monetary union (EMU) against 36 percent in favour, Finnish news agency STT reported on Thursday, citing a new opinion poll.</p>
<p>It did not make clear if the remaining 20 percent were undecided. The poll was carried out by research company Taloustutkimus for the Conservative Party's Verkkouutiset paper, STT said, adding that attitudes had not changed much during spring.</p>
<p>The poll covered 2,000 people, it said, but did not say when it was carried out.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
